import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AboutPlainLead from '../../components/AboutPlainLead.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={"Writing a Game Once and Running It Everywhere: Where Exact Replay Ends and Tolerance Begins"}
  description={"About: Writing a Game Once and Running It Everywhere. All nine falsifier suites executed (GE-H1 through GE-H9): 0/25,500 3-OS × 3-ISA Q32.32 SHA-256 mismatches (GE-H1); 3-OS UCRT/libm/glibc and cross-ISA FMA float drift (GE-H2); 28/28 hardware DirectX 12/Metal/Vulkan GPU×API pairs passing tolerance (GE-H3); -76.22% SLOC vs Unity C# across 17 behavior Forms (GE-H4); 10,000-actor scaling at 0.058–0.125 ms/tick on compiled projections vs 390-actor Python ceiling (GE-H5); 98.46% recall / F1 = 0.9922 across 260 interface modules vs 0.1159 parse-only baseline (GE-H6); 840-trajectory Lyapunov sweep R^2_mean >= 0.994 (GE-H7); 0/6,480 mismatches across three 1-hour 216,000-tick 3-OS replays from 44.6 KB gzip logs (GE-H8); and 36/36 headless Godot 4.7.2 state-trace parity (GE-H9)."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Writing a Game Once and Running It Everywhere: Where Exact Replay Ends and Tolerance Begins
    </h1>
    <AboutPlainLead id="game-engines" />
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study asks whether a game can be written once as a checked state machine and then projected across languages, operating systems, CPU instruction set architectures, and GPU rendering stacks. Both the surveyed specifications and all nine executed falsifier suites (Section 6, <code>GE-H1</code> through <code>GE-H9</code>) establish the boundary: <strong>yes</strong> for game rules, interface contracts, and long-horizon simulation under pinned integer arithmetic (<code>GE-H1</code>, <code>GE-H4</code>, <code>GE-H5</code>, <code>GE-H6</code>, <code>GE-H8</code>, and <code>GE-H9</code>); <strong>no</strong> when standard library transcendentals or fused multiply-add lowering cross OS/compiler/ISA boundaries in chaotic collisions, where divergence time scales linearly with <code>ln(Δ / δ₀)</code> (<code>GE-H2</code> and <code>GE-H7</code>); and <strong>no</strong> for bit-exact pixels across graphics APIs and vendors, yet <strong>yes</strong> under a checked perceptual tolerance gate (<code>GE-H3</code> across <code>8</code> hardware <code>GPU × API</code> endpoints spanning Windows <code>DirectX 12</code>, Apple <code>Metal</code>, and Linux/Windows <code>Vulkan</code>; <code>measured_j = None</code>, <code>board_metered = false</code>).
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">In plain words</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Under <code>Q32.32</code> 64-bit integer physics (<code>GE-H1</code>, <code>100,000</code> ticks), a 16-body 2D arena replays bit-for-bit across native Rust, C++20 (Clang, GCC, and Windows MSVC <code>cl.exe</code>), WebAssembly, Node.js <code>BigInt</code>, and Python across six machines spanning macOS, Linux, and Windows 11 (<code>0 / 25,500</code> <code>SHA-256</code> mismatches; <code>0.073–13.60 J</code> macOS <code>L3</code> <code>reported_j</code>; <code>1.89–181.87 J</code> Linux <code>L2</code> RAPL package <code>reported_j</code>; <code>138.9M–24,722.2M</code> Win32 <code>L3</code> CPU cycles).</li>
        <li>Under IEEE 754 floating-point physics (<code>GE-H2</code>, <code>25,000</code> ticks; <code>GE-H7</code>, <code>840</code> paired trajectories across <code>δ₀ ∈ [2⁻⁵², 2⁻¹⁰]</code>), all three desktop OS math libraries diverge pairwise on <code>std::sin</code>/<code>std::cos</code> at ticks <code>10–37</code> without <code>-ffast-math</code>, while macroscopic divergence time follows <code>t* = (1 / Λ) ln(Δ / δ₀)</code> across three chaotic templates (<code>Λ̂ = 2.48</code>, <code>5.07</code>, and <code>1.95 s⁻¹</code>; cell-mean <code>R² = 0.9940–0.9995</code>, <code>p ≤ 10⁻⁷⁷</code>).</li>
        <li>Across eight hardware <code>GPU × API</code> endpoints on headless <code>wgpu</code> (<code>GE-H3</code>, <code>512×512</code> <code>RGBA8Unorm</code> across <code>DirectX 12</code>, <code>Metal</code>, and <code>Vulkan</code>), even switching <code>DirectX 12</code> vs <code>Vulkan</code> on the same Windows 11 GPU alters <code>1</code> LSB via shader lowering, yet all <code>28 / 28</code> hardware endpoint pairs pass perceptual tolerance (<code>PSNR ≥ 64.16 dB</code>, <code>SSIM ≥ 0.99983</code>, <code>Δ_max ≤ 2</code>).</li>
        <li>Across <code>17</code> reference gameplay modules spanning <em>Haunted Jaunt</em>, <em>Survival Shooter</em>, and <em>Tanks</em> (<code>GE-H4</code>, <code>0 / 680</code> cross-language trace mismatches), admitted <code>.rce</code> Forms cut behavior <code>SLOC</code> by <code>76.22%</code> vs Unity <code>MonoBehaviour</code> C# (<code>72.50%</code> including embedded <code>intent</code> proofs, <code>92.51%</code> boilerplate glue cut), <code>61.47%</code> vs Bevy Rust ECS, and <code>51.99%</code> vs Godot 4 GDScript, while compiled Form projections (<code>GE-H5</code>) sustain <code>10,000</code> actors in <code>0.0583 ms</code> (<code>C++20 -O3</code>, <code>1.694 mJ/tick</code> Linux <code>L2</code> RAPL), <code>0.0724 ms</code> (<code>Wasm32</code>), and <code>0.1248 ms</code> (<code>Rust -O3</code>) vs Python's <code>390</code>-actor <code>20 ms</code> ceiling (<code>7,728×</code> lower socket energy at <code>N = 10,000</code>).</li>
        <li>Static Form + four-edge scene/asset manifest checking (<code>GE-H6</code>, <code>260</code> modules across <code>26</code> defect families, zero runtime ticks) achieves <code>98.46%</code> recall, <code>100.0%</code> precision, and <code>F1 = 0.9922</code> vs <code>F1 = 0.1159</code> on untyped <code>godot --headless --check-only</code>; three one-hour (<code>216,000</code>-tick) sessions replay with <code>0 / 6,480</code> <code>SHA-256</code> mismatches across macOS <code>arm64</code>, Linux <code>x86_64</code>, and Windows 11 <code>x86_64</code> from <code>44.6 KB</code> gzip input logs alone (<code>GE-H8</code>, <code>116×–292×</code> smaller than gzip state snapshots, whereas all <code>4</code> ambient-leak controls fail at tick <code>1</code>); and <code>form_to_gdscript.py</code> achieves <code>36 / 36</code> (<code>100.0%</code>) headless Godot 4.7.2 parity across <code>18,000</code> ticks (<code>GE-H9</code>). Explore all six interactive instruments and the playable <code>Q32.32</code> Chrono-Budget Arena at <a href="/living/game-engines/" class="text-brand-cyan underline">/living/game-engines/</a>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/game-engines/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read → /papers/game-engines/
